How'd you do that, Grandpa?

01:04:15.450 --> 01:04:17.730
A magician isn't supposed to reveal his tricks.

01:04:18.480 --> 01:04:20.440
Oh, I have a joke.

01:04:20.970 --> 01:04:21.810
Go for it.

01:04:22.180 --> 01:04:22.800
Knock, knock.

01:04:23.340 --> 01:04:24.260
Who's there?

01:04:24.850 --> 01:04:25.470
Isidore.

01:04:25.810 --> 01:04:26.670
Isidore who?

01:04:27.540 --> 01:04:29.140
Is a doorbell ringing, Grandpa?

01:04:33.420 --> 01:04:35.600
That was a good one, Caillou.

01:04:36.140 --> 01:04:39.020
And now for my famous Christmas apple pie.

01:04:39.380 --> 01:04:42.640
Even better than Grandpa's famous turkey stuffing.

01:04:43.570 --> 01:04:45.410
We wish you a Merry Christmas.

01:04:45.510 --> 01:04:47.450
We wish you a Merry Christmas.

01:04:47.750 --> 01:04:49.430
We wish you a Merry Christmas.

01:04:49.630 --> 01:04:51.310
And a Happy New Year.

01:04:52.090 --> 01:04:57.160
What do you say we go outside and see how our lights look, Caillou?

01:04:58.800 --> 01:04:59.020
Yes.

01:05:01.560 --> 01:05:02.340
Ready, Caillou?

01:05:03.270 --> 01:05:03.470
Ready!

01:05:04.140 --> 01:05:05.560
Okay, here goes!

01:05:06.500 --> 01:05:14.960
I'm gonna wait up all night to see Santa.

01:05:15.490 --> 01:05:17.430
But Santa won't come if you're awake.

01:05:19.230 --> 01:05:23.180
Do you want to see what's behind the big Christmas Eve window?

01:05:23.740 --> 01:05:24.140
Yeah!

01:05:30.380 --> 01:05:37.220
Twas the night before Christmas, when all through the house, not a creature was stirring, not even a mouse.

01:05:37.850 --> 01:05:43.710
The stockings were hung by the chimney with care, in hopes that St. Nicholas soon would be there.

01:05:44.360 --> 01:05:49.800
The children were nestled all snug in their beds, while visions of sugar plums danced in their heads.

01:05:50.320 --> 01:05:56.840
And Mama in her kerchief, and I in my cap, had just settled down for a long winter's nap,

01:05:57.110 --> 01:05:59.610
when out on the lawn there arose such a clatter!

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:02.400
I sprang from the bed to see what was the matter.

01:06:02.990 --> 01:06:05.270
Away to the window, I flew like a flash,

01:06:05.650 --> 01:06:08.190
tore open the shutters, and threw up the sash.

01:06:08.560 --> 01:06:11.560
When what to my wondering eyes should appear

01:06:11.560 --> 01:06:15.850
but a miniature sleigh and eight tiny reindeer.

01:06:16.230 --> 01:06:19.450
With a little old driver so lively and quick,

01:06:19.650 --> 01:06:22.540
I knew in a moment it must be St. Nick.

01:06:22.940 --> 01:06:25.480
No, Dasher! Now, Dancer!

01:06:25.680 --> 01:06:27.760
Now, Prancer and Vixen!

01:06:28.130 --> 01:06:29.970
On, Comet! On, Comet!

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:32.380
Hubert, on Donner and Blitzen.

01:06:33.650 --> 01:06:36.190
And then in a twinkling, I heard on the roof

01:06:36.190 --> 01:06:38.900
the prancing and pawing of each little hoof.

01:06:39.630 --> 01:06:42.030
As I drew in my hand and was turning around,

01:06:42.550 --> 01:06:45.170
down the chimney St. Nicholas came with a bound.

01:06:45.530 --> 01:06:49.220
His eyes, how they twinkled, his dimples, how merry.

01:06:49.720 --> 01:06:52.580
His cheeks were like roses, his nose like a cherry.

01:06:53.110 --> 01:06:55.610
He spoke not a word, but went straight to his work

01:06:55.610 --> 01:06:58.940
and filled all the stockings, then turned with a jerk

01:06:59.320 --> 01:06:59.980
and laid...

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:07.090
his finger aside of his nose and giving a nod up the chimney he rose he sprang to his sleigh

01:07:07.090 --> 01:07:13.660
to his team gave a whistle and away they all flew like the down of a thistle but i heard him

01:07:13.660 --> 01:07:24.310
exclaim ere he drove out of sight happy christmas to all and to all a good night sweet dreams caillou

01:07:38.510 --> 01:07:43.910
He was excited to see all the presents, and he noticed that Santa had eaten all his cookies.

01:07:49.830 --> 01:07:50.310
I...

01:07:52.000 --> 01:07:52.880
Presents first?

01:07:55.780 --> 01:07:57.840
All right, your presents first.

01:07:58.300 --> 01:07:58.920
Here, Mommy.

01:08:00.380 --> 01:08:00.980
Here, Daddy.

01:08:01.540 --> 01:08:02.640
Thank you, sweetheart.

01:08:03.300 --> 01:08:04.560
When did you make these?

01:08:05.060 --> 01:08:06.260
It was a surprise.

01:08:06.480 --> 01:08:08.420
I made them at Leo's house.

01:08:08.940 --> 01:08:11.540
And the wrapping is so beautiful.

01:08:12.140 --> 01:08:12.620
Open it.

01:08:13.960 --> 01:08:16.600
What a beautiful picture.

01:08:17.270 --> 01:08:18.450
It's you, Mommy.

01:08:18.860 --> 01:08:20.300
And is this a picture of me?

01:08:20.740 --> 01:08:21.240
Yes.

01:08:21.830 --> 01:08:22.410
Thank you.

01:08:22.670 --> 01:08:23.110
It's wonderful.

01:08:23.920 --> 01:08:25.680
And this is for you, Rosie.

01:08:26.150 --> 01:08:27.090
Rosie Puss?

01:08:28.670 --> 01:08:29.050
Nope.

01:08:30.410 --> 01:08:31.370
Do you like it?

01:08:31.820 --> 01:08:36.760
I think Santa brought this one for you.

01:08:47.320 --> 01:08:49.020
Now, see a present.

01:08:49.630 --> 01:08:50.370
How nice.

01:08:50.700 --> 01:08:51.360
Thank you.

01:08:51.560 --> 01:08:52.850
Thank you, Rosie.

01:08:53.880 --> 01:08:55.060
Well, look at this.

01:08:55.200 --> 01:08:56.580
You're missing slippers.

01:08:58.260 --> 01:08:58.940
Oops.

01:08:59.340 --> 01:08:59.980
And you're...

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:11.830
electric toothbrush. Here you go. Caillou present. You weren't lost at all. Now I get it.

01:09:12.140 --> 01:09:21.430
Rosie wanted to give us presents we love. Rexy. You two did a very good job at keeping your

01:09:21.430 --> 01:09:27.600
presents a surprise. And I think Rosie just started our very own family tradition. Caillou

01:09:27.600 --> 01:09:29.960
learned a lot about traditions from all the...

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:35.780
stories, right Caillou? Uh-huh. I learned about the first Christmas tree and where Christmas

01:09:35.780 --> 01:09:41.890
cards came from and St. Nick. He taught us that giving and sharing are important, right?

01:09:42.330 --> 01:09:56.650
Right. Gilbert. Oh, Rosie. Gilbert present. Christmas, Gilbert. Dear Daddy, it's from Santa.

01:09:58.480 --> 01:09:59.980
Just what I need.

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:05.380
It's Christmas morning and it's snowy winter.

01:10:05.420 --> 01:10:11.200
It's Christmas morning and our families cheer together.

01:10:12.160 --> 01:10:17.820
They share our day that I don't care.

01:10:18.500 --> 01:10:22.520
We watch and feel that Christmas air.

01:10:23.020 --> 01:10:26.180
The love that's in our stay with.

01:10:31.370 --> 01:10:38.170
Christmas morning and it's snowy winter

01:10:39.350 --> 01:10:40.770
Christmas morning

01:11:01.240 --> 01:11:01.740
Christmas.

01:11:31.950 --> 01:11:32.210
Thank you.

01:12:02.560 --> 01:12:03.160
Okay.
